data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":765,"item_id":"msg_044d9de8c042d56c016b0319268ce887d188ffd64b0abc4684","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"cedar-4\",\"decision\":\"reuse\",\"ability\":\"probe\",\"reason\":\"The implemented probe capability already provides non-ingestive observation and small-sample physical trials. Its function, inputs and costs match this request; the reported reference failures require a reference-resolution repair, not a duplicate investigation ability. Inspection of the owned sample is feasible without equipment, but cannot establish nutritional value, absence of toxins or preparation requirements.\",\"specification\":\"Reuse probe and hand its reference-resolution defect to the current implementation conversation. Accept target='item:item-48-cedar-4-1203' through the shared item-reference resolver; resolve the persistent item ID against authoritative current state, validate ownership and remaining quantity, and preserve origin and history. An owned inventory item is accessible without requiring a ground-object observation entry; ground items still require actual visibility and interaction distance under shared geometry. Never substitute a resource prototype, invent a sample or silently choose another item. Public schema: probe({target:string, mode:'observe'|'trial', test?:string}); retain compatible existing parameters. For mode='observe', perform one round of non-ingestive external examination at 0.2 energy, consuming no material. Report only physically observable represented features, current observable deterioration and observation limits; provenance may be reported as retained records, not as a newly measured fact. Do not reveal hidden nutrition or toxicity fields as analytical results. A valid owned reference must not fail merely because it is absent from observedObjectIds. Trial mode retains the existing one-round, 0.5-energy, 0.1-unit cost, but must validate an explicit executable physical test, actual required implements and exposure constraints before reserving or consuming anything; no ingestion, hazardous exposure, imaginary assay or unsupported safety certification. External inspection is the immediately executable precursor. Commit observation or trial effects once, with an idempotent operation ID; record actual cost, consumed quantity, findings, unresolved questions and evidence IDs in personal knowledge. Failed validation costs no material. No persistent work or escrow is needed for the one-round inspection; death before execution cancels it without effects. Any existing trial implementation spanning rounds must retain actual remaining work, pause safely and cancel on death, releasing unconsumed actor-owned escrow once while preserving consumed material and completed changes. Reuse existing event and knowledge infrastructure separately from this resolver repair. Implementation and review advance no simulation time and grant no mastery or stock.\",\"experienceReview\":\"A genuinely informative examination may support the existing grounded-understanding source, not a new aliased reward. Emit trial-result for a completed examination and information-confirmed only when actual evidence establishes a previously unresolved, personally new observable fact; qualified=true must reference that evidence and must not mean that food safety has been established. The participant is the examining actor. Apply the registered 0.8 amount, cap 1, eight-round hold, refresh repetition and 12-round cooldown; maintained satisfaction uses the existing 0.035 gain and 0.0015 decay under its registered qualification and cooldown semantics. Reinspection of the same fact, successful reference resolution alone, requesting and learning earn nothing. There is no separate pleasure award: the supported benefit here is resolving real uncertainty, not an established enjoyable sensory experience. Health, hunger and protected mental accounts remain unchanged except for